WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.346
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:09.700
RYAN MATSUMOTO: Welcome to
the Quick Start Tutorial

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.770
for the Data Loss
Prevention API.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.510
In this video,
we're going to walk

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.239
through how to get started
with the DLP API, which allows

00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:18.400
you to discover,
classify, and protect

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.990
your most sensitive data.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.840
To start, make sure you have
a Google Cloud project set up

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.660
in the Google Cloud platform
Console with billing enabled.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.490
You can either
create a new project

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.440
or use an existing project.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.720
Next, enable the DLP API.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.470
In the Navigation menu,
click on APIs and Services.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:39.960
Click the Enable APIs and
Services button at the top.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.350
Search for Data Loss Prevention
and select it from the results.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.990
On the DLP API
page, click Enable

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.060
to enable it for the project.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.330
Now set up a service account
for authentication purposes.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:58.230
In the Navigation menu, click on
IAM and Admin Service Accounts.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:02.200
Click Create Service
Account at the top.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.855
Give your service account
a name and click Create.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:13.600
Give your service account the
Role of Cloud DLP, DLP User.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.940
Click Continue and then Done.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.520
On the right side of your
screen, click the three dots

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.110
icon for the service
account you just created

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:22.780
and click Create Key.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.910
Then click Create.

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.970
This will download a service
account key JSON file

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:29.800
to your computer.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.020
From command line, set
the environment variable

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.030
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS
to point to the JSON file

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.968
you just downloaded.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:41.260
Now you will download some
sample code to your computer

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.880
from command line using Git.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.860
Once the repository
has been cloned,

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:49.460
navigate to nodejs-dlp/samples.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:51.770
From here, install
app dependencies

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:54.080
by running npm install.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.140
This will download various
packages, including the DLP

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:59.630
Client Library for Node.js.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.650
Next, set the environment
variable GCLOUD_PROJECT

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.630
to your Google Cloud project ID.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.750
Now run the code in
inspectString.js.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.760
This code inspects
an input string

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.980
with the DLP API
for sensitive data

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.165
and logs it to our console.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.310
For this example, the
script finds two pieces

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.840
of potentially sensitive data,
a name and an email address.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:25.680
And that's it.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.130
Make sure to check out the rest
of our DLP API documentation

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:32.430
to learn more about how to
discover, classify, and protect

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:33.510
your most sensitive data.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:36.860
[MUSIC PLAYING]

